# Citation metadata for this repository (Citation File Format 1.2.0).

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this toolkit in your research, please cite this repository and
  the architecture paper it models (Zhou et al., NANOARCH '23, the first entry
  under references).
title: "STRATUM: an integrated memristor process-in-memory chip toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A device-to-chip simulation toolkit for memristor-based in-memory
  computing. It models a pulse-programmed memristor, single-device and
  crossbar-level non-idealities, ADC/DAC and digital peripherals, and a
  three-level chip organisation (tile / processing unit / array) driven by a
  RISC-V-like vector instruction workflow. Workloads include an MNIST MLP
  compiled to that instruction set, ResNet-18 and VGG-16 with
  hardware-aware training, and a detection task, all scored through the same
  datapath arithmetic. A Tkinter front-end exposes every simulation
  parameter and produces self-contained HTML reports.
type: software

authors:
  - name: "IMChip B.V."
    email: "contact@imchip.nl"

version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sagarneel1107/STRATUM"
license: Apache-2.0

# DOI under which this work can be cited.
# doi: ""

